2026-10-20T21:06:14.6965512Z +             markdown: '# Unused global variable\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6966248Z +               'A global (module-level) variable is defined (by an assignment) but never used and is not explicitly made public by inclusion in the `__all__` list.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6966489Z -             markdown: '# Returning tuples with varying lengths\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6967546Z -               'A common pattern for functions returning multiple arguments is to return a single tuple containing said arguments. If the function has multiple return points, care must be taken to ensure that the tuples returned have the same length.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6967634Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6969163Z +               'It is sometimes necessary to have a variable which is not used. These unused variables should have distinctive names, to make it clear to readers of the code that they are deliberately not used. The most common conventions for indicating this are to name the variable `_` or to start the name of the variable with `unused` or `_unused`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6969247Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6969635Z +               'The query accepts the following names for variables that are intended to be unused:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6969733Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6969949Z +               '* Any name consisting entirely of underscores.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6970129Z +               '* Any name containing `unused`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6970300Z +               '* The names `dummy` or `empty`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6970499Z +               '* Any "special" name of the form `__xxx__`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6971302Z +               'Variables that are defined in a group, for example `x, y = func()` are handled collectively. If they are all unused, then this is reported. Otherwise they are all treated as used.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6971397Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6971485Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6971610Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6972709Z +               'If the variable is included for documentation purposes or is otherwise intentionally unused, then change its name to indicate that it is unused, otherwise delete the assignment (taking care not to delete right hand side if it has side effects).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6973093Z -               'Ensure that the function returns tuples of similar lengths.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6973182Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6973260Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6973376Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6974334Z +               'In this example, the `random_no` variable is never read but its assignment has a side effect. Because of this it is important to only remove the left hand side of the assignment in line 9.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6975683Z -               'In this example, the `sum_length_product1` function simultaneously calculates the sum, length, and product of the values in the given list. For empty lists, however, the returned tuple only contains the sum and length of the list. In `sum_length_product2` this error has been corrected.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6975781Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6975868Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6975974Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6976108Z +               'import random\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6976280Z -               'def sum_length_product1(l):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6976409Z -               '    if l == []:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6976718Z -               '        return 0, 0                              # this tuple has the wrong length\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6976843Z -               '    else:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6976976Z -               '        val = l[0]\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6977367Z -               '        restsum, restlength, restproduct = sum_length_product1(l[1:])\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6977654Z -               '        return restsum + val, restlength + 1, restproduct * val\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6977800Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6977976Z +               'def write_random_to_file():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6978150Z +               '    no = random.randint(1, 10)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6978353Z +               '    with open("random.txt", "w") as file:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6978515Z +               '        file.write(str(no))\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6978643Z +               '    return no\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6978812Z -               'def sum_length_product2(l):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6978944Z -               '    if l == []:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6979257Z -               '        return 0, 0, 1                           # this tuple has the correct length\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6979383Z -               '    else:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6979526Z -               '        val = l[0]\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6979828Z -               '        restsum, restlength, restproduct = sum_length_product2(l[1:])\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6980101Z -               '        return restsum + val, restlength + 1, restproduct * val\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6980190Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6980376Z +               'random_no = write_random_to_file()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.6980467Z                 '```\n' +
