2026-10-20T21:06:14.7007869Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7008077Z +             markdown: '# Explicit export is not defined\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7009389Z +               'When a module is imported using `import *`, all attributes listed in `__all__` are imported. If `__all__` includes attributes that are not defined in the module then an exception is triggered. This usually indicates a typographic error in the attributes in `__all__` or in the name of the object.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7009725Z -             markdown: '# Explicit returns mixed with implicit (fall through) returns\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7011294Z -               'When a function contains both explicit returns (`return value`) and implicit returns (where code falls off the end of a function), this often indicates that a return statement has been forgotten. It is best to return an explicit return value even when returning `None` because this makes it easier for other developers to read your code.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7011451Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7011536Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7011658Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7012548Z +               'Correct any typographic errors, either in the name of the object or in the string in `__all__`. If there are no typographic errors, either delete the name from `__all__` or add the object to the module.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7012793Z -               'Add an explicit return at the end of the function.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7012874Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7012959Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7013072Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7014074Z +               'In the example, the function name `spam` has been misspelled in the `__all__` list. This will result in `spamm` being highlighted as an undefined export. Correcting the spelling will fix the defect.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7014953Z -               'In the `check_state1` function, the developer probably did intend to use an implicit return value of `None` as this equates to `False`. However, the function in `check_state2` is easier to read.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7015046Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7015127Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7015240Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7015445Z +               "__all__ = ['spamm', 'troll', 'paywall']\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7015667Z -               '    def check_state1(state, interactive=True):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7015891Z -               "        if not state['good'] or not state['bad']:\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7016153Z -               '            if (good or bad or skip or reset) and interactive:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7016469Z -               '                return                                          # implicitly return None\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7016648Z -               "            if not state['good']:\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7016977Z -               "                raise util.Abort(_('cannot bisect (no known good revisions)'))\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7017118Z -               '            else:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7017437Z -               "                raise util.Abort(_('cannot bisect (no known bad revisions)')) \n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7017782Z -               '        return True  \t\t\t\t\t\t\t                              \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7017915Z -               '           \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7018138Z -               '    def check_state2(state, interactive=True):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7018352Z -               "        if not state['good'] or not state['bad']:\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7018609Z -               '            if (good or bad or skip or reset) and interactive:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7019005Z -               '                return False                                    # return an explicit value\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7019177Z -               "            if not state['good']:\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7019498Z -               "                raise util.Abort(_('cannot bisect (no known good revisions)'))\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7019638Z -               '            else:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7019955Z -               "                raise util.Abort(_('cannot bisect (no known bad revisions)'))\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7020099Z -               '        return True\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7020185Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7020347Z +               "def spam(): return 'Spam'\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7020514Z +               "def troll(): return 'Troll'\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7020692Z +               "def paywall(): return 'Pay wall'\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7020791Z +               '\n' +
