2026-10-20T21:06:14.7102052Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7102372Z +             markdown: '# Mismatch between signature and use of an overridden method\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7103528Z +               'There is a call to the overriding method, and potentially the overridden method, with arguments that are not legal for the overridden method. This will cause an error if the overridden method is called and is a violation of the Liskov substitution principle.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7103888Z -             markdown: '# Use of a print statement at module level\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7104907Z -               'Using `print` statements in level scope may result in surprising output at import time. This in turn means that other code cannot safely import the module in question if the program may only write real output to standard out.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7104996Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7105081Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7105200Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7105677Z +               'Ensure that the overridden method accepts all the parameters that are legal for overriding method(s).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7106155Z -               'Replace the `print` statements with calls to some form of logging function or use the `warnings` module.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7106236Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7106329Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7106443Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7107995Z +               'In this example there is a mismatch between the legal parameters for the base class method `(self, source, filename)` and the extension method `(self, source)`. Since there is a call that uses the signature of the extension method then it can be inferred that the base signature is erroneous and should be updated to match that of the extension method.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7108649Z -               'In the example, importing the module may cause a message to be printed, which may interfere with the operation of the program.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7108735Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7108816Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7108930Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7109017Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7109238Z +               'class BaseClass(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7109344Z -               'try:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7109519Z -               '    import fast_system as system\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7109676Z -               'except ImportError:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7109983Z -               '    print ("Cannot import fast system, falling back on slow system")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7110156Z -               '    import slow_system as system\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7110242Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7110486Z +               '    def run(self, source, filename, symbol="single"):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7110631Z +               '        ... # Definition\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7110766Z -               '#Fixed version\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7110901Z -               'import logging\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7110981Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7111236Z +               '    def load_and_run(self, filename):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7111431Z +               '        source = self.load(filename)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7111806Z +               '        self.run(source) # Matches signature in derived class, but not in this class.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7111972Z -               'try:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7112140Z -               '    import fast_system as system\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7112292Z -               'except ImportError:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7112632Z -               '    logging.info("Cannot import fast system, falling back on slow system")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7112799Z -               '    import slow_system as system\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7112886Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7113060Z +               'class DerivedClass(BaseClass):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7113149Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7113311Z +               '    def run(self, source):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7113460Z +               '        ... # Definition\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7113552Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7113642Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7114251Z +               'The base method should be updated to either remove the `filename` parameters, or add a default value for it.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7114343Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7114438Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7114549Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7115403Z +               '* Wikipedia: [Liskov Substitution Principle](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liskov_substitution_principle), [Method overriding](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Method_overriding#Python).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7115704Z +             text: '# Mismatch between signature and use of an overridden method\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7116860Z +               'There is a call to the overriding method, and potentially the overridden method, with arguments that are not legal for the overridden method. This will cause an error if the overridden method is called and is a violation of the Liskov substitution principle.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7117456Z -               '* Python Language Reference: [The print statement](http://docs.python.org/2/reference/simple_stmts.html#the-print-statement).\n' +
