2026-10-20T21:06:14.7149404Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7149517Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7150071Z +               '* Python Language Reference: [Function definitions](http://docs.python.org/2/reference/compound_stmts.html#function).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7150288Z +             text: '# Returning tuples with varying lengths\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7151345Z +               'A common pattern for functions returning multiple arguments is to return a single tuple containing said arguments. If the function has multiple return points, care must be taken to ensure that the tuples returned have the same length.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7152391Z -               '* Python Language Reference: [The for statement](http://docs.python.org/reference/compound_stmts.html#the-for-statement), [object.__iter__](http://docs.python.org/2.7/reference/datamodel.html#object.__iter__).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7152910Z -               '* Python Standard Library: [Iterator types](http://docs.python.org/dev/library/stdtypes.html#iterator-types).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7153639Z -               '* Scipy lecture notes: [Iterators, generator expressions and generators](http://scipy-lectures.github.io/advanced/advanced_python/#iterators).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7153973Z -             text: '# Non-iterable used in for loop\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7154966Z -               'The `for` statement is designed to allow you to iterate over the elements of a sequence or other iterable object. If a non-iterable object is used in a `for` statement (`for var in object:`) then a TypeError will be raised.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7155052Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7155139Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7155263Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7155537Z +               'Ensure that the function returns tuples of similar lengths.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7156171Z -               'Since this defect usually indicates a logical error, it is not possible to give a general method for addressing the defect.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7156264Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7156352Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7156466Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7157738Z +               'In this example, the `sum_length_product1` function simultaneously calculates the sum, length, and product of the values in the given list. For empty lists, however, the returned tuple only contains the sum and length of the list. In `sum_length_product2` this error has been corrected.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7158527Z -               'In this example, the loop may attempt to iterate over `None`, which is not an iterable. It is likely that the programmer forgot to test for `None` before the loop.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7158615Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7158703Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7158808Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7158975Z +               'def sum_length_product1(l):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7159111Z +               '    if l == []:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7159415Z +               '        return 0, 0                              # this tuple has the wrong length\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7159540Z +               '    else:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7159676Z +               '        val = l[0]\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7159984Z +               '        restsum, restlength, restproduct = sum_length_product1(l[1:])\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7160258Z +               '        return restsum + val, restlength + 1, restproduct * val\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7160338Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7160504Z +               'def sum_length_product2(l):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7160635Z +               '    if l == []:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7160940Z +               '        return 0, 0, 1                           # this tuple has the correct length\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7161064Z +               '    else:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7161202Z +               '        val = l[0]\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7161501Z +               '        restsum, restlength, restproduct = sum_length_product2(l[1:])\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7161771Z +               '        return restsum + val, restlength + 1, restproduct * val\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7161856Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7162037Z -               'def illegal_for_loop(seq = None):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7162176Z -               '    for x in seq:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7162381Z -               '        print (x)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7162477Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7162572Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7162658Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7162743Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7162863Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7163405Z +               '* Python Language Reference: [Function definitions](http://docs.python.org/2/reference/compound_stmts.html#function).\n'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7164566Z -               '* Python Language Reference: [The for statement](http://docs.python.org/reference/compound_stmts.html#the-for-statement), [object.__iter__](http://docs.python.org/2.7/reference/datamodel.html#object.__iter__).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7165086Z -               '* Python Standard Library: [Iterator types](http://docs.python.org/dev/library/stdtypes.html#iterator-types).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7165750Z -               '* Scipy lecture notes: [Iterators, generator expressions and generators](http://scipy-lectures.github.io/advanced/advanced_python/#iterators).\n'
