2026-10-20T21:06:14.7197549Z +               '* Python Standard Library: [Iterator Types](https://docs.python.org/3/library/stdtypes.html#typeiter).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7197779Z +             text: '# `__iter__` method returns a non-iterator\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7198076Z +               'The `__iter__` method of a class should always return an iterator.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7198162Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7198983Z +               'Iterators must implement both `__next__` and `__iter__` for Python 3, or both `next` and `__iter__` for Python 2. The `__iter__` method of the iterator must return the iterator object itself.\n' +
