2026-10-20T21:06:14.7208143Z -           help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7208331Z -             markdown: '# Statement has no effect\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7208926Z -               'An expression statement without side effects is just clutter. It confuses the reader and may have a slight impact on performance.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7209024Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7209119Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7209238Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7209606Z +               'Make sure the value returned by `__iter__` implements the full iterator protocol.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7210626Z -               'First determine what the intention of the code was, if there is no intention of a side effect, then just delete the statement. However, it is probable that there is a mistake in the code and some effect was intended.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7210711Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7212226Z -               'This query will not flag a statement consisting solely of a string as having no side effect, as these are often used as comments. If you want to use strings as comments, the most common convention is to use triple quoted strings rather than single quoted ones. Although consistency is more important than conforming to any particular style.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7212378Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7212470Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7212585Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7213998Z +               'In this example, we have implemented our own version of `range`, extending the normal functionality with the ability to skip some elements by using the `skip` method. However, the iterator `MyRangeIterator` does not fully implement the iterator protocol (namely it is missing `__iter__`).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7214380Z -               'In this example neither line of the `increment_and_show()` function has any effect.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7214466Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7215523Z +               "Iterating over the elements in the range seems to work on the surface, for example the code `x = sum(my_range)` gives the expected result. However, if we run `sum(iter(my_range))` we get a `TypeError: 'MyRangeIterator' object is not iterable`.\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7216065Z -               'The first line, `++x`, has no effect as it applies the unary plus operator twice. Probably the programmer intended `x += 1`\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7216150Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7216731Z +               'If we try to skip some elements using our custom method, for example `y = sum(my_range.skip({6,9}))`, this also raises a `TypeError`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7217168Z -               'The second line, `x.show`, has no observable effect, but it is likely that `x.show()` was intended.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7217257Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7217554Z +               'The fix is to implement the `__iter__` method in `MyRangeIterator`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7217635Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7217728Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7217838Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7218068Z +               'class MyRange(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7218248Z +               '    def __init__(self, low, high):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7218393Z +               '        self.low = low\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7218537Z +               '        self.high = high\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7218621Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7218766Z +               '    def __iter__(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7218996Z +               '        return MyRangeIterator(self.low, self.high)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7219158Z -               'def increment_and_show(x):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7219256Z -               '    ++x\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7219453Z -               '    x.show\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7219540Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7219705Z +               '    def skip(self, to_skip):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7219970Z +               '        return MyRangeIterator(self.low, self.high, to_skip)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7220072Z -               '```\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7220237Z -             text: '# Statement has no effect\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7220812Z -               'An expression statement without side effects is just clutter. It confuses the reader and may have a slight impact on performance.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7220891Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7221065Z +               'class MyRangeIterator(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7221278Z +               '    def __init__(self, low, high, skip=None):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7221429Z +               '        self.current = low\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7221644Z +               '        self.high = high\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7221799Z +               '        self.skip = skip\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7221880Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7222027Z +               '    def __next__(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7222276Z +               '        if self.current >= self.high:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7222441Z +               '            raise StopIteration\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7222612Z +               '        to_return = self.current\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7222759Z +               '        self.current += 1\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7222976Z +               '        if self.skip and to_return in self.skip:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7223149Z +               '            return self.__next__()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7223291Z +               '        return to_return\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7223437Z -               '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7224479Z -               'First determine what the intention of the code was, if there is no intention of a side effect, then just delete the statement. However, it is probable that there is a mistake in the code and some effect was intended.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7224564Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7224793Z +               '    # Problem is fixed by uncommenting these lines\n' +
