2026-10-20T21:06:14.7274280Z +             markdown: '# Mismatch between signature and use of an overriding method\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7275397Z +               'There is a call to the overridden method, and potentially the overriding method, with arguments that are not legal for the overriding method. This will cause an error if the overriding method is called and is a violation of the Liskov substitution principle.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7275586Z -             markdown: '# Use of exit() or quit()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7276765Z -               'The `exit` and `quit` "functions" are actually `site.Quitter` objects and are loaded, at interpreter start up, from `site.py`. However, if the interpreter is started with the `-S` flag, or a custom `site.py` is used then `exit` and `quit` may not be present.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7276856Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7276945Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7277074Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7277547Z +               'Ensure that the overriding method accepts all the parameters that are legal for the overridden method.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7278092Z -               'Replace uses of `exit()` and `quit()` with `sys.exit()` which is built into the interpreter and is guaranteed to be present.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7278177Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7278257Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7278372Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7280385Z +               'In this example there is a mismatch between the legal parameters for the base class method `(self, source, filename, symbol)` and the extension method `(self, source)`. The extension method can be used to override the base method as long as values are not specified for the `filename` and (optional) `symbol` parameters. If the extension method was passed the additional parameters accepted by the base method then an error would occur.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7280856Z -               'In this example, `exit()` is used and will fail if the interpreter is passed the `-S` option.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7280945Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7281028Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7281135Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7281221Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7281383Z +               'class BaseClass(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7281509Z -               'def main():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7281633Z -               '    try:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7281773Z -               '        process()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7281942Z -               '    except Exception as ex:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7282081Z -               '        print(ex)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7282210Z -               '        exit(1)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7282298Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7282541Z +               '    def run(self, source, filename, symbol="single"):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7282689Z +               '        ... # Definition\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7282789Z -               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7283238Z -               'In this example, `sys.exit()` is used and will behave the same regardless of the interpreter options.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7283318Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7283509Z +               '    def load_and_run(self, filename):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7283689Z +               '        source = self.load(filename)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7284261Z +               '        self.run(source, filename) # Matches signature in this class, but not in the derived class.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7284349Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7284524Z +               'class DerivedClass(BaseClass):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7284650Z -               '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7284779Z -               'import sys\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7284859Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7285105Z +               '    def run(self, source):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7285256Z +               '        ... # Definition\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7285380Z -               'def main():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7285500Z -               '    try:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7285637Z -               '        process()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7285807Z -               '    except Exception as ex:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7285946Z -               '        print(ex)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7286085Z -               '        sys.exit(1)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7286173Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7286263Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7286906Z +               'The extension method should be updated to support the `filename` and `symbol` parameters supported by the overridden method.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7286995Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7287092Z +               '\n' +
