2026-10-20T21:06:14.7309745Z             fullDescription: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7310418Z +             text: 'The return value of a procedure (a function that does not return a value) is used. This is confusing to the reader as the value (None) has no meaning.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7311028Z -             text: 'Using a Break or Return statement in a finally block causes the Try-finally block to exit, discarding the exception.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7311114Z             },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7311196Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7311442Z +             markdown: '# Use of the return value of a procedure\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7312514Z +               'All functions in Python return a value. If a function has no `return` statements or none of the `return` statements return a value then the function will return `None`. However, this value has no meaning and should be ignored.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7312758Z -             markdown: "# 'break' or 'return' statement in finally\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7313963Z -               'When a `break` or `return` statement is used in a `finally` block this causes the `try-finally` block to exit immediately discarding the exception. This is unlikely to be the intention of the developer and makes the code more difficult to read.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7314059Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7314588Z +               "Using the return value of such a 'procedure' is confusing to the reader as it suggests that the value is significant.\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7314676Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7314823Z -               '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7315469Z -               'Either move the `break` or `return` statement to immediately after the `finally` block or use an explicit `except` block to handle the exception.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7315558Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7316076Z -               'These modifications are behavior changing so you must take care to ensure that the resulting behavior is correct.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7316169Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7316265Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7316399Z -               '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7317761Z -               '* Python Language Reference: [ The try statement](http://docs.python.org/2.7/reference/compound_stmts.html#the-try-statement), [ The break statement](http://docs.python.org/2/reference/simple_stmts.html#break), [ The return statement](http://docs.python.org/2/reference/simple_stmts.html#return).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7318180Z -               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-584](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/584.html).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7318408Z -             text: "# 'break' or 'return' statement in finally\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7319565Z -               'When a `break` or `return` statement is used in a `finally` block this causes the `try-finally` block to exit immediately discarding the exception. This is unlikely to be the intention of the developer and makes the code more difficult to read.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7319662Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7319758Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7319878Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7320421Z +               'Do not use the return value of a procedure; replace `x = proc()` with `proc()` and replace any use of the value with `None`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7321131Z -               'Either move the `break` or `return` statement to immediately after the `finally` block or use an explicit `except` block to handle the exception.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7321218Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7321739Z -               'These modifications are behavior changing so you must take care to ensure that the resulting behavior is correct.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7321827Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7321953Z +               '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7322630Z +               'In this example, the `my_print` function is a procedure as it returns no value of any meaning. Using the return value is misleading in subsequent code.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7322719Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7322846Z -               '## References\n' +
