2026-10-20T21:06:14.7367906Z +             text: '`__init__` method is a generator.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7368281Z -             text: "Using 'return' or 'yield' outside a function causes a 'SyntaxError' at runtime."
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7368359Z             },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7368511Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7368722Z +             markdown: '# `__init__` method is a generator\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7369966Z +               'The `__init__` method of a class is used to initialize new objects, not create them. As such, it should not return any value. By including a `yield` expression in the method turns it into a generator method. On calling it will return a generator resulting in a runtime error.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7370234Z -             markdown: "# Use of 'return' or 'yield' outside a function\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7371130Z -               'In Python, `return` and `yield` statements and the `yield from` expression can only be used within a function. Using them outside a function or a class method results in a `SyntaxError` at runtime.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7371215Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7371302Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7371428Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7372020Z +               'The presence of a `yield` expression in an `__init__` method suggests a logical error, so it is not possible to suggest a general fix.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7372743Z -               'Using these elements outside a function or a class method usually indicates an error in the logic. Consequently, it is not possible to suggest a general fix.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7372829Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7372908Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7373021Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7373561Z +               'In this example the `__init__` method contains a yield expression. This is not logical in the context of an initializer.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7376792Z -               'In this example, a `return` statement is used outside a class method in a class and a `yield` statement is used outside a function in a scope of a module which would result in a `SyntaxError` when running this code. In this example, the invalid class could be corrected by placing the `return` statement in a class method, or by refactoring the class into a function. The invalid `yield` statement could become part of a new generator function containing the `for` loop.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7377138Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7377290Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7377484Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7377826Z +               'class InitIsGenerator(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7378128Z +               '    def __init__(self, i):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7378408Z +               '        yield i\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7378824Z -               '# invalid class with return outside a function\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7379140Z -               'class InvalidClass1(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7379388Z -               '    if [1, 2, 3]:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7379879Z -               '        return "Exists"\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7380072Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7380524Z -               '# invalid statement with yield outside a function\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7380808Z -               'for i in [1, 2, 3]:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7381049Z -               '    yield i\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7381229Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7381390Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7381538Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7381760Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7382661Z +               '* Python: [The __init__ method](http://docs.python.org/3/reference/datamodel.html#object.__init__).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7383048Z +             text: '# `__init__` method is a generator\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7385749Z +               'The `__init__` method of a class is used to initialize new objects, not create them. As such, it should not return any value. By including a `yield` expression in the method turns it into a generator method. On calling it will return a generator resulting in a runtime error.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7386905Z -               '* Python reference: [ The return statement](https://docs.python.org/3.7/reference/simple_stmts.html#the-return-statement).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7388026Z -               '* Python reference: [ The yield statement](https://docs.python.org/3.7/reference/simple_stmts.html#yield).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7388931Z -               '* Python PEP-380: [ The yield from expression](https://docs.python.org/3/whatsnew/3.3.html#pep-380).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7389394Z -             text: "# Use of 'return' or 'yield' outside a function\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7390965Z -               'In Python, `return` and `yield` statements and the `yield from` expression can only be used within a function. Using them outside a function or a class method results in a `SyntaxError` at runtime.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7391145Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7391298Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7391532Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7392665Z +               'The presence of a `yield` expression in an `__init__` method suggests a logical error, so it is not possible to suggest a general fix.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7394304Z -               'Using these elements outside a function or a class method usually indicates an error in the logic. Consequently, it is not possible to suggest a general fix.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7394501Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7394650Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7394864Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7395869Z +               'In this example the `__init__` method contains a yield expression. This is not logical in the context of an initializer.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7399805Z -               'In this example, a `return` statement is used outside a class method in a class and a `yield` statement is used outside a function in a scope of a module which would result in a `SyntaxError` when running this code. In this example, the invalid class could be corrected by placing the `return` statement in a class method, or by refactoring the class into a function. The invalid `yield` statement could become part of a new generator function containing the `for` loop.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7400191Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7400361Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7400577Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7400936Z +               'class InitIsGenerator(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7401250Z +               '    def __init__(self, i):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7401513Z +               '        yield i\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7401960Z -               '# invalid class with return outside a function\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7402296Z -               'class InvalidClass1(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7402565Z -               '    if [1, 2, 3]:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7403052Z -               '        return "Exists"\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7403240Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7403696Z -               '# invalid statement with yield outside a function\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7404215Z -               'for i in [1, 2, 3]:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7404464Z -               '    yield i\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7404657Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7404824Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7404986Z                 '\n' +
