2026-10-20T21:06:14.7419242Z             },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7419381Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7419868Z +             markdown: '# Iterator does not return self from `__iter__` method\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7422097Z +               'Iterator classes (classes defining a `__next__` method) should have an `__iter__` method that returns the iterator itself. This ensures that the object is also an iterable; and behaves as expected when used anywhere an iterator or iterable is expected, such as in `for` loops.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7422407Z -             markdown: '# Unreachable code\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7423177Z -               'Unreachable code makes the code more difficult to understand and may slow down loading of modules.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7423349Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7423504Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7423716Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7424921Z +               'Ensure that the `__iter__` method returns `self`, or is otherwise equivalent as an iterator to `self`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7427021Z -               'Deleting the unreachable code will make the code clearer and preserve the meaning of the code. However, it is possible that the original intention was that the code should execute and that it is unreachable signifies some other error.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7427209Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7427349Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7427533Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7428991Z +               "In the following example, the `MyRange` class's `__iter__` method does not return `self`. This would lead to unexpected results when used with a `for` loop or `in` statement.\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7430120Z -               'In this example the assignment to `remainder` is never reached because there is a ` return` statement on the previous line.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7430309Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7430465Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7430683Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7430991Z +               'class MyRange(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7431327Z +               '    def __init__(self, low, high):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7431627Z +               '        self.current = low\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7431933Z +               '        self.high = high\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7432181Z -               'import math\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7432338Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7432630Z +               '    def __iter__(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7433230Z +               '        return (self.current, self.high) # BAD: does not return `self`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7433521Z -               'def my_div(x, y):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7434108Z -               '    return math.floor(x / y)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7434518Z -               '    remainder = x - math.floor(x / y) * y\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7434684Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7434975Z +               '    def __next__(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7435337Z +               '        if self.current > self.high:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7435630Z +               '            return None\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7435944Z +               '        self.current += 1\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7436298Z +               '        return self.current - 1\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7436488Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7436644Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7436871Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7437902Z +               '* Python Language Reference: [object.__iter__](http://docs.python.org/3/reference/datamodel.html#object.__iter__).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7439054Z +               '* Python Standard Library: [Iterators](http://docs.python.org/3/library/stdtypes.html#typeiter).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7439597Z +             text: '# Iterator does not return self from `__iter__` method\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7441966Z +               'Iterator classes (classes defining a `__next__` method) should have an `__iter__` method that returns the iterator itself. This ensures that the object is also an iterable; and behaves as expected when used anywhere an iterator or iterable is expected, such as in `for` loops.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7442912Z -               '* Wikipedia: [Unreachable Code](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unreachable_code).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7443769Z -               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-561](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/561.html).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7444378Z -             text: '# Unreachable code\n' +
