2026-10-20T21:06:14.7499692Z -             text: "Using a 'delete' statement to delete a local variable is unnecessary, because the variable is deleted automatically when the function exits."
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7499784Z             },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7499878Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7500233Z +             markdown: '# Explicit returns mixed with implicit (fall through) returns\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7501837Z +               'When a function contains both explicit returns (`return value`) and implicit returns (where code falls off the end of a function), this often indicates that a return statement has been forgotten. It is best to return an explicit return value even when returning `None` because this makes it easier for other developers to read your code.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7502110Z -             markdown: '# Unnecessary delete statement in function\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7503228Z -               'Passing a local variable to a `del` statement results in that variable being removed from the local namespace. When exiting a function all local variables are deleted, so it is unnecessary to explicitly delete variables in such cases.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7503323Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7503413Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7503544Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7504039Z +               'Add an explicit return at the end of the function.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7504359Z -               'Remove the `del` statement.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7504449Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7504542Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7504666Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7505582Z +               'In the `check_state1` function, the developer probably did intend to use an implicit return value of `None` as this equates to `False`. However, the function in `check_state2` is easier to read.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7506844Z -               'In the function below, the variable `x` is assigned a value that is used for a calculation, and is then explicitly deleted before the function exits. In this case, the delete statement can be removed without changing the behavior of the function.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7506953Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7507044Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7507170Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7507422Z +               '    def check_state1(state, interactive=True):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7507667Z +               "        if not state['good'] or not state['bad']:\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7507960Z +               '            if (good or bad or skip or reset) and interactive:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7508319Z +               '                return                                          # implicitly return None\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7508511Z +               "            if not state['good']:\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7508881Z +               "                raise util.Abort(_('cannot bisect (no known good revisions)'))\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7509094Z +               '            else:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7509461Z +               "                raise util.Abort(_('cannot bisect (no known bad revisions)')) \n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7509758Z +               '        return True  \t\t\t\t\t\t\t                              \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7509957Z +               '           \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7510204Z +               '    def check_state2(state, interactive=True):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7510452Z +               "        if not state['good'] or not state['bad']:\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7510742Z +               '            if (good or bad or skip or reset) and interactive:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7511118Z +               '                return False                                    # return an explicit value\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7511311Z +               "            if not state['good']:\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7511666Z +               "                raise util.Abort(_('cannot bisect (no known good revisions)'))\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7511820Z +               '            else:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7512180Z +               "                raise util.Abort(_('cannot bisect (no known bad revisions)'))\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7512336Z +               '        return True\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7512523Z -               'def unnecessary_delete():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7512701Z -               '    x = get_some_object()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7512867Z -               '    do_calculation(x)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7513164Z -               '    del x                       # This del statement is unnecessary\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7513257Z                 '\n' +
