2026-10-20T21:06:14.7650101Z -             text: 'Assigning multiple variables without ensuring that you define a value for each variable causes an exception at runtime.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7650228Z -           },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7650379Z -           help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7650722Z -             markdown: '# Mismatch in multiple assignment\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7652878Z -               'An assignment statement evaluates a sequence expression and assigns each item of the sequence to one of the variables on the left. If there is a mismatch between the number of variables on the left and the values in the sequence on the right of the statement, then an exception is raised at runtime.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7653046Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7653188Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7653388Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7655758Z +               'If the method always raises as exception, then if it is intended to be an abstract method, the `@abstractmethod` decorator should be used. Otherwise, ensure that the method raises an exception of the correct type, or remove the method if the operation does not need to be supported.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7656328Z -               'Ensure that the number of variables on either side of the assignment match.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7656468Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7656599Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7656767Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7658806Z +               'In the following example, the `__add__` method of `A` raises a `TypeError` if `other` is of the wrong type. However, it should return `NotImplemented` instead of rising an exception, to allow other classes to support adding to `A`. This is demonstrated in the class `B`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7660186Z -               'The following examples show a simple definition of the Fibonacci series. In the first example, one of the values in the assignment has been duplicated, causing an exception at runtime.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7660324Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7660456Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7660628Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7660823Z +               'class A:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7661079Z +               '    def __init__(self, a):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7661297Z +               '        self.a = a \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7661539Z -               '# Fibonacci series 1:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7661975Z -               '# the sum of two elements defines the next\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7662108Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7662378Z +               '    def __add__(self, other):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7662815Z +               '        # BAD: Should return NotImplemented instead of raising\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7663197Z +               '        if not isinstance(other,A):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7663640Z +               '            raise TypeError(f"Cannot add A to {other.__class__}")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7664099Z +               '        return A(self.a + other.a)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7664620Z -               'a, b = 0, 1, 1  # Assignment fails: accidentally put three values on right\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7664833Z -               'while b < 10:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7665034Z -               '     print b\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7665257Z -               '     a, b = b, a+b\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7665384Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7665576Z +               'class B:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7665832Z +               '    def __init__(self, a):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7666051Z +               '        self.a = a \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7666281Z -               '# Fibonacci series 2:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7666608Z -               '# the sum of two elements defines the next\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7667188Z -               'a, b = 0, 1   # Assignment succeeds: two variables on left and two values on right\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7667393Z -               'while b < 10:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7667594Z -               '     print b\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7667803Z -               '     a, b = b, a+b\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7667935Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7668196Z +               '    def __add__(self, other):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7669356Z +               '        # GOOD: Returning NotImplemented allows for the operation to fallback to other implementations to allow other classes to support adding to B.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7669662Z +               '        if not isinstance(other,B):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7669947Z +               '            return NotImplemented\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7670220Z +               '        return B(self.a + other.a)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7670382Z +               '    \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7670535Z -               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7670661Z                 '\n' +
