2026-10-20T21:06:14.7744884Z +             markdown: '# Deprecated slice method\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7746076Z +               'The `__getslice__`, `__setslice__` and `__delslice__` methods have been deprecated since Python 2.0. In general, no class should implement these methods.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7746490Z -             markdown: '# Unnecessary pass\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7748890Z -               'A `pass` statement is only necessary when it is the only statement in a block (the list of statements forming part of a compound statement). This is because the purpose of the ` pass` statement is to allow empty blocks where they would otherwise be syntactically invalid. If the block already contains other statements then the `pass` statement is unnecessary.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7749013Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7750663Z +               'The only exceptions to this rule are classes that inherit from `list` and override `__getitem__`, `__setitem__` or `__delitem__`. Since `list` implements the slicing methods any class inheriting from `list` must implement the the slicing methods to ensure correct behavior of `__getitem__`, `__setitem__` and `__delitem__`. These exceptions to the rule will not be treated as violations.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7750753Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7750850Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7750980Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7751453Z +               'Delete the slicing method. Any functionality should be moved to the equivalent `__xxxitem__` method:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7751630Z -               'Remove the `pass` statement.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7751717Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7751960Z +               '* `__getslice__` should be replaced with `__getitem__`\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7752201Z +               '* `__setslice__` should be replaced with `__setitem__`\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7752441Z +               '* `__delslice__` should be replaced with `__delitem__`\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7752533Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7752659Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7753547Z +               '* Python Language Reference: [ Additional methods for emulation of sequence types](https://docs.python.org/2/reference/datamodel.html#additional-methods-for-emulation-of-sequence-types).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7753727Z +             text: '# Deprecated slice method\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7754844Z +               'The `__getslice__`, `__setslice__` and `__delslice__` methods have been deprecated since Python 2.0. In general, no class should implement these methods.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7755257Z -               '* Python: [pass](http://docs.python.org/2/tutorial/controlflow.html#pass-statements).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7755425Z -             text: '# Unnecessary pass\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7757073Z -               'A `pass` statement is only necessary when it is the only statement in a block (the list of statements forming part of a compound statement). This is because the purpose of the ` pass` statement is to allow empty blocks where they would otherwise be syntactically invalid. If the block already contains other statements then the `pass` statement is unnecessary.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7757169Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7758813Z +               'The only exceptions to this rule are classes that inherit from `list` and override `__getitem__`, `__setitem__` or `__delitem__`. Since `list` implements the slicing methods any class inheriting from `list` must implement the the slicing methods to ensure correct behavior of `__getitem__`, `__setitem__` and `__delitem__`. These exceptions to the rule will not be treated as violations.\n' +
