2026-10-20T21:06:14.7767240Z             fullDescription: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7767727Z +             text: '`__del__` methods may be called at arbitrary times, perhaps never called at all, and should be simple.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7767968Z -             text: 'An exception object is created, but is not used.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7768052Z             },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7768136Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7768350Z +             markdown: '# Overly complex `__del__` method\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7769279Z +               'The `__del__` method exists to release any resources held by an object when that object is deleted. The `__del__` is called only by the garbage collector which may call it after an indefinite delay or never.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7769465Z -             markdown: '# Unused exception object\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7770118Z -               'Creating a new exception object is no different from creating any other object. The exception needs to be raised to have an effect.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7770217Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7770907Z +               'Consequently, `__del__` method should not be relied on to release resources, such as file descriptors. Rather, these resources should be released explicitly.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7771058Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7771640Z +               'The existence of a complex `__del__` method suggests that this is the main or only way to release resources associated with the object.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7771737Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7771837Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7771969Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7772558Z +               'In order to ensure correct cleanup of the object add an explicit close(), or similar, method. Possibly make the object a context manager.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7772762Z -               'Insert a `raise` before the exception.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7772855Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7773064Z +               'The __del__ method should just call close()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7773151Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7773251Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7773364Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7774352Z +               'The first example below shows a class which relies on `__del__` to release resources. The second example shows an improved version of the class where `__del__` simply calls close.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7775286Z -               "In this example, the first function `do_action_forgotten_raise()` silently ignores any erroneous input. Whereas, the second function `do_action` correctly raises an exception if the 'action' is not understood.\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7775369Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7775458Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7775564Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7775651Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7775922Z +               '#Relies on __del__ being called by the garbage collector.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7776090Z +               'class CachedPreferencesFile\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7776289Z -               'def do_action_forgotten_raise(action):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7776449Z -               '    if action == "go":\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7776579Z -               '        start()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7776839Z -               '    elif action == "stop":\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7776974Z -               '        stop()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7777094Z -               '    else:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7777254Z -               '        ValueError(action)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7777335Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7777442Z +               '    ...\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7777598Z -               'def do_action(action):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7777742Z -               '    if action == "go":\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7777878Z -               '        start()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7778040Z -               '    elif action == "stop":\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7778236Z -               '        stop()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7778367Z -               '    else:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7778546Z -               '        raise ValueError(action)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7778630Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7778783Z +               '    def __del__(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7779027Z +               '        for key, value in self.preferences.items():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7779226Z +               '            self.write_pair(key, value)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7779398Z +               '        self.backing.close()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7779493Z -               '```\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7779671Z -             text: '# Unused exception object\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7780277Z -               'Creating a new exception object is no different from creating any other object. The exception needs to be raised to have an effect.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7780358Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7780510Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7780660Z +               '#Better version\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7780827Z +               'class CachedPreferencesFile\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7780975Z -               '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7781237Z -               'Insert a `raise` before the exception.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7781327Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7781429Z +               '    ...\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7781510Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7781661Z +               '    def close(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7781895Z +               '        for key, value in self.preferences.items():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7782079Z +               '            self.write_pair(key, value)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7782247Z +               '        self.backing.close()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7782377Z -               '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7783326Z -               "In this example, the first function `do_action_forgotten_raise()` silently ignores any erroneous input. Whereas, the second function `do_action` correctly raises an exception if the 'action' is not understood.\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7783412Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7783565Z +               '    def __del__(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7783706Z +               '        self.close()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7783991Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7784110Z +               '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7784241Z -               '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7784327Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7784457Z +               '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7784998Z +               '* Python Standard Library: [Context manager](http://docs.python.org/library/stdtypes.html#context-manager-types).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7785200Z +             text: '# Overly complex `__del__` method\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7786110Z +               'The `__del__` method exists to release any resources held by an object when that object is deleted. The `__del__` is called only by the garbage collector which may call it after an indefinite delay or never.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7786309Z -               'def do_action_forgotten_raise(action):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7786466Z -               '    if action == "go":\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7786595Z -               '        start()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7786845Z -               '    elif action == "stop":\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7786979Z -               '        stop()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7787098Z -               '    else:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7787258Z -               '        ValueError(action)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7787339Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7788064Z +               'Consequently, `__del__` method should not be relied on to release resources, such as file descriptors. Rather, these resources should be released explicitly.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7788222Z -               'def do_action(action):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7788367Z -               '    if action == "go":\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7788564Z -               '        start()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7788729Z -               '    elif action == "stop":\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7788855Z -               '        stop()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7788983Z -               '    else:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7789160Z -               '        raise ValueError(action)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7789246Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7789845Z +               'The existence of a complex `__del__` method suggests that this is the main or only way to release resources associated with the object.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7789940Z -               '```\n'
