2026-10-20T21:06:14.7909062Z             fullDescription: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7909493Z +             text: "Handling 'BaseException' means that system exits and keyboard interrupts may be mis-handled."
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7909898Z -             text: 'Calculating the length of the hypotenuse using the standard formula may lead to overflow.'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7909985Z             },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7910074Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7910297Z +             markdown: "# Except block handles 'BaseException'\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7911840Z +               'All exception classes in Python derive from `BaseException`. `BaseException` has three important subclasses, `Exception` from which all errors and normal exceptions derive, `KeyboardInterrupt` which is raised when the user interrupts the program from the keyboard and `SystemExit` which is raised by the `sys.exit()` function to terminate the program.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7912133Z -             markdown: '# Pythagorean calculation with sub-optimal numerics\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7913589Z -               'Calculating the length of the hypotenuse using the standard formula `c = sqrt(a**2 + b**2)` may lead to overflow if the two other sides are both very large. Even though `c` will not be much bigger than `max(a, b)`, either `a**2` or `b**2` (or both) will. Thus, the calculation could overflow, even though the result is well within representable range.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7913674Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7914352Z +               'Since `KeyboardInterrupt` and `SystemExit` are special they should not be grouped together with other `Exception` classes.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7914445Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7915583Z +               'Catching `BaseException`, rather than its subclasses may prevent proper handling of `KeyboardInterrupt` or `SystemExit`. It is easy to catch `BaseException` accidentally as it is caught implicitly by an empty `except:` statement.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7915682Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7915778Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7915900Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7916377Z +               'Handle `Exception`, `KeyboardInterrupt` and `SystemExit` separately. Do not use the plain `except:` form.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7916845Z -               'Rather than `sqrt(a**2 + b**2)`, use the built-in function `hypot(a,b)` from the `math` library.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7916937Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7917022Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7917131Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7918493Z +               'In these examples, a function `application.main()` is called that might raise `SystemExit`. In the first two functions, `BaseException` is caught, but this will discard `KeyboardInterrupt`. In the third function, `call_main_program_fixed` only `SystemExit` is caught, leaving `KeyboardInterrupt` to propagate.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7919248Z -               'The following code shows two different ways of computing the hypotenuse. The first is a direct rewrite of the Pythagorean theorem, the second uses the built-in function.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7919338Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7919626Z +               'In these examples `KeyboardInterrupt` is accidentally ignored.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7919775Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7919871Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7919985Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7920257Z -               '# We know that a^2 + b^2 = c^2, and wish to use this to compute c\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7920488Z -               'from math import sqrt, hypot\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7920581Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7920848Z +               'def call_main_program_implicit_handle_base_exception():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7920966Z +               '    try:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7921204Z +               '        #application.main calls sys.exit() when done.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7921369Z +               '        application.main()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7921527Z +               '    except Exception as ex:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7921661Z +               '        log(ex)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7921786Z +               '    except:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7921916Z +               '        pass\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7922070Z -               'a = 3e154 # a^2 > 1e308\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7922213Z -               'b = 4e154 # b^2 > 1e308\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7922436Z -               '# with these, c = 5e154 which is less that 1e308\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7922523Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7922772Z +               'def call_main_program_explicit_handle_base_exception():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7922896Z +               '    try:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7923127Z +               '        #application.main calls sys.exit() when done.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7923285Z +               '        application.main()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7923443Z +               '    except Exception as ex:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7923572Z +               '        log(ex)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7923734Z +               '    except BaseException:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7923983Z +               '        pass\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7924135Z -               'def longSideDirect():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7924360Z -               '    return sqrt(a**2 + b**2) # this will overflow\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7924445Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7924615Z +               'def call_main_program_fixed():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7924739Z +               '    try:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7924968Z +               '        #application.main calls sys.exit() when done.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7925204Z +               '        application.main()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7925363Z +               '    except Exception as ex:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7925491Z +               '        log(ex)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7925644Z +               '    except SystemExit:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7925770Z +               '        pass\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7925860Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7926013Z -               'def longSideBuiltin():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7926262Z -               '    return hypot(a, b) # better to use built-in function\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7926348Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7926432Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7926616Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7927483Z +               '* Python Language Reference: [The try statement](http://docs.python.org/3/reference/compound_stmts.html#try), [Exceptions](http://docs.python.org/3/reference/executionmodel.html#exceptions).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7927925Z +               "* M. Lutz, Learning Python, Section 35.3: Exception Design Tips and Gotchas, O'Reilly Media, 2013.\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7928347Z +               '* Python Tutorial: [Errors and Exceptions](https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/errors.html).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7928747Z +               '* Common Weakness Enumeration: [CWE-396](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/396.html).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7928963Z +             text: "# Except block handles 'BaseException'\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7930575Z +               'All exception classes in Python derive from `BaseException`. `BaseException` has three important subclasses, `Exception` from which all errors and normal exceptions derive, `KeyboardInterrupt` which is raised when the user interrupts the program from the keyboard and `SystemExit` which is raised by the `sys.exit()` function to terminate the program.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7931115Z -               '* Python Language Reference: [The hypot function](https://docs.python.org/library/math.html#math.hypot)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7931393Z -               '* Wikipedia: [Hypot](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hypot).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7931655Z -             text: '# Pythagorean calculation with sub-optimal numerics\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7933099Z -               'Calculating the length of the hypotenuse using the standard formula `c = sqrt(a**2 + b**2)` may lead to overflow if the two other sides are both very large. Even though `c` will not be much bigger than `max(a, b)`, either `a**2` or `b**2` (or both) will. Thus, the calculation could overflow, even though the result is well within representable range.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7933191Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7933745Z +               'Since `KeyboardInterrupt` and `SystemExit` are special they should not be grouped together with other `Exception` classes.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7933963Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7934984Z +               'Catching `BaseException`, rather than its subclasses may prevent proper handling of `KeyboardInterrupt` or `SystemExit`. It is easy to catch `BaseException` accidentally as it is caught implicitly by an empty `except:` statement.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7935085Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7935173Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7935298Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7935775Z +               'Handle `Exception`, `KeyboardInterrupt` and `SystemExit` separately. Do not use the plain `except:` form.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7936176Z -               'Rather than `sqrt(a**2 + b**2)`, use the built-in function `hypot(a,b)` from the `math` library.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7936263Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7936348Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7936456Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7937809Z +               'In these examples, a function `application.main()` is called that might raise `SystemExit`. In the first two functions, `BaseException` is caught, but this will discard `KeyboardInterrupt`. In the third function, `call_main_program_fixed` only `SystemExit` is caught, leaving `KeyboardInterrupt` to propagate.\n' +
