2026-10-20T21:06:14.7959336Z -               'If the class specified in an `except` handler (within a `try` statement) is not a legal exception class, then it will never match a raised exception and never be executed\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7959422Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7959599Z -               'Legal exception classes are:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7959688Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7959891Z -               '* Any old-style classes (Python 2 only)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7960206Z -               '* Any subclass of the builtin class `BaseException`\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7960825Z -               'However, it recommended that you only use subclasses of the builtin class `Exception` (which is itself a subclass of `BaseException`).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7960927Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7961026Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7961151Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7961376Z +               'Ensure all exceptions are handled correctly.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7962067Z -               'Ensure that the specified class is the one intended. If it is not then replace it with the correct one. Otherwise the entire `except` block can be deleted.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7962150Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7962235Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7962353Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7962916Z +               'In this example, the program keeps running with the same privileges if it fails to drop to lower privileges.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7963007Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7963102Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7963277Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7963381Z +               '# ...\n' +
