2026-10-20T21:06:14.7985102Z +             markdown: '# Raising `NotImplemented`\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7986527Z +               'The constant `NotImplemented` is not an `Exception`, but is often confused for `NotImplementedError`. If it is used as an exception, such as in `raise NotImplemented` or `raise NotImplemented("message")`, a `TypeError` will be raised rather than the expected `NotImplemented`. This may make debugging more difficult.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7986692Z -             markdown: '# Illegal raise\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7987223Z -               'If the object raised is not a legal Exception class or an instance of one, then a `TypeError` will be raised instead.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7987312Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7988165Z +               '`NotImplemented` should only be used as a special return value for implementing special methods such as `__lt__`. Code that is not intended to be called should raise `NotImplementedError`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7988340Z -               'Legal exception classes are:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7988427Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7988631Z -               '* Any old-style classes (Python 2 only)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7988869Z -               '* Any subclass of the builtin class `BaseException`\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7989483Z -               'However, it recommended that you only use subclasses of the builtin class `Exception` (which is itself a subclass of `BaseException`).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7989570Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7989660Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7989789Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7990767Z +               'If a `NotImplementedError` is intended to be raised, replace the use of `NotImplemented` with that. If `NotImplemented` is intended to be returned rather than raised, replace the `raise` with `return NotImplemented`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7991102Z -               'Change the expression in the `raise` statement to be a legal exception.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7991260Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7991340Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7991462Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7992149Z +               'In the following example, the method `wrong` will incorrectly raise a `TypeError` when called. The method `right` will raise a `NotImplementedError`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7992231Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7992327Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7992440Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7992644Z -               '#Cannot raise an int, even if we want to\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7992853Z -               'def raise_int():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7993028Z -               '    #Will raise a TypeError\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7993155Z -               '    raise 4\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7997769Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7997999Z +               'class Abstract(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7998107Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7998270Z +               '    def wrong(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7998452Z +               '        # Will raise a TypeError\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7998640Z +               '        raise NotImplemented()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7998738Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7998887Z +               '    def right(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7999089Z +               '        raise NotImplementedError()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7999188Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7999276Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.7999486Z                 '\n' +
