2026-10-20T21:06:14.8053933Z             },
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8054030Z             help: {
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8054228Z +             markdown: '# Unreachable `except` block\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8055400Z +               'When handling an exception, Python searches the except blocks in source code order until it finds a matching `except` block for the exception. An except block, `except E:`, specifies a class `E` and will match any exception that is an instance of `E`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8055639Z -             markdown: "# Except block handles 'BaseException'\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8057181Z -               'All exception classes in Python derive from `BaseException`. `BaseException` has three important subclasses, `Exception` from which all errors and normal exceptions derive, `KeyboardInterrupt` which is raised when the user interrupts the program from the keyboard and `SystemExit` which is raised by the `sys.exit()` function to terminate the program.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8057362Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8058585Z +               'If a more general except block precedes a more specific except block, then the more general block is always executed and the more specific block is never executed. An except block, `except A:`, is more general than another except block, `except B:`, if `A` is a super class of `B`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8059138Z -               'Since `KeyboardInterrupt` and `SystemExit` are special they should not be grouped together with other `Exception` classes.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8059222Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8059716Z +               'For example: `except Exception:` is more general than `except Error:` as `Exception` is a super class of `Error`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8060737Z -               'Catching `BaseException`, rather than its subclasses may prevent proper handling of `KeyboardInterrupt` or `SystemExit`. It is easy to catch `BaseException` accidentally as it is caught implicitly by an empty `except:` statement.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8060821Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8060904Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8061024Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8061824Z +               'Reorganize the `except` blocks so that the more specific `except` is defined first. Alternatively, if the more specific `except` block is no longer required, then it should be deleted.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8062309Z -               'Handle `Exception`, `KeyboardInterrupt` and `SystemExit` separately. Do not use the plain `except:` form.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8062389Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8062476Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8062591Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8063187Z +               'In the following example, the `except Exception:` will handle `AttributeError` preventing the subsequent handler from ever executing.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8064741Z -               'In these examples, a function `application.main()` is called that might raise `SystemExit`. In the first two functions, `BaseException` is caught, but this will discard `KeyboardInterrupt`. In the third function, `call_main_program_fixed` only `SystemExit` is caught, leaving `KeyboardInterrupt` to propagate.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8064833Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8065123Z -               'In these examples `KeyboardInterrupt` is accidentally ignored.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8065208Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8065378Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8065490Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8065575Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8065838Z -               'def call_main_program_implicit_handle_base_exception():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8065955Z -               '    try:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8066194Z -               '        #application.main calls sys.exit() when done.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8066361Z -               '        application.main()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8066519Z -               '    except Exception as ex:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8066651Z -               '        log(ex)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8066774Z -               '    except:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8066903Z -               '        pass\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8066989Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8067164Z +               'def incorrect_except_order(val):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8067488Z -               'def call_main_program_explicit_handle_base_exception():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8067600Z                 '    try:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8067734Z +               '        val.attr\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8067884Z +               '    except Exception:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8068109Z +               '        print ("Exception")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8068266Z +               '    except AttributeError:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8068438Z +               '        print ("AttributeError")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8068550Z +               '        \n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8068784Z -               '        #application.main calls sys.exit() when done.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8068988Z -               '        application.main()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8069147Z -               '    except Exception as ex:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8069281Z -               '        log(ex)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8069441Z -               '    except BaseException:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8069564Z -               '        pass\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8069652Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8069828Z -               'def call_main_program_fixed():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8069944Z -               '    try:\n' +
