2026-10-20T21:06:14.8100524Z +             markdown: "# Non-exception in 'except' clause\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8101259Z +               'If the class specified in an `except` handler (within a `try` statement) is not a legal exception class, then it will never match a raised exception and never be executed\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8101410Z -             markdown: '# Empty except\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8103080Z -               'Ignoring exceptions that should be dealt with in some way is almost always a bad idea. The loss of information can lead to hard to debug errors and incomplete log files. It is even possible that ignoring an exception can cause a security vulnerability. An empty `except` block may be an indication that the programmer intended to handle the exception, but never wrote the code to do so.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8103172Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8103342Z +               'Legal exception classes are:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8103427Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8103624Z +               '* Any old-style classes (Python 2 only)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8103980Z +               '* Any subclass of the builtin class `BaseException`\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8104577Z +               'However, it recommended that you only use subclasses of the builtin class `Exception` (which is itself a subclass of `BaseException`).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8104721Z -               '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8104935Z -               'Ensure all exceptions are handled correctly.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8105021Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8105104Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8105228Z -               '## Example\n' +
