2026-10-20T21:06:14.8118899Z -             markdown: '# Raising `NotImplemented`\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8120379Z -               'The constant `NotImplemented` is not an `Exception`, but is often confused for `NotImplementedError`. If it is used as an exception, such as in `raise NotImplemented` or `raise NotImplemented("message")`, a `TypeError` will be raised rather than the expected `NotImplemented`. This may make debugging more difficult.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8120472Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8121322Z -               '`NotImplemented` should only be used as a special return value for implementing special methods such as `__lt__`. Code that is not intended to be called should raise `NotImplementedError`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8121481Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8121576Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8121721Z -               '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8122689Z -               'If a `NotImplementedError` is intended to be raised, replace the use of `NotImplemented` with that. If `NotImplemented` is intended to be returned rather than raised, replace the `raise` with `return NotImplemented`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8122784Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8122880Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8123006Z -               '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8123695Z -               'In the following example, the method `wrong` will incorrectly raise a `TypeError` when called. The method `right` will raise a `NotImplementedError`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8123899Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8124003Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8124131Z -               '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8124224Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8124386Z -               'class Abstract(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8124483Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8124627Z -               '    def wrong(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8124804Z -               '        # Will raise a TypeError\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8124978Z -               '        raise NotImplemented()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8125071Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8125219Z -               '    def right(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8125403Z -               '        raise NotImplementedError()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8125503Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8125596Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8125677Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8125795Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8126320Z +               '* Python Language Reference: [Exceptions](https://docs.python.org/reference/executionmodel.html#exceptions).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8126821Z +               '* Python Tutorial: [Handling Exceptions](https://docs.python.org/tutorial/errors.html#handling-exceptions).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8127108Z +             text: "# Non-exception in 'except' clause\n" +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8127867Z +               'If the class specified in an `except` handler (within a `try` statement) is not a legal exception class, then it will never match a raised exception and never be executed\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8128509Z -               '* Python Language Reference: [The NotImplementedError exception](https://docs.python.org/library/exceptions.html#NotImplementedError).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8129167Z -               '* Python Language Reference: [The NotImplemented constant](https://docs.python.org/3/library/constants.html#NotImplemented).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8129793Z -               '* Python Language Reference: [Emulating numeric types](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/datamodel.html#emulating-numeric-types).\n',
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8129968Z -             text: '# Raising `NotImplemented`\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8131389Z -               'The constant `NotImplemented` is not an `Exception`, but is often confused for `NotImplementedError`. If it is used as an exception, such as in `raise NotImplemented` or `raise NotImplemented("message")`, a `TypeError` will be raised rather than the expected `NotImplemented`. This may make debugging more difficult.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8131475Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8131648Z +               'Legal exception classes are:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8132559Z -               '`NotImplemented` should only be used as a special return value for implementing special methods such as `__lt__`. Code that is not intended to be called should raise `NotImplementedError`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8132650Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8132850Z +               '* Any old-style classes (Python 2 only)\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8133155Z +               '* Any subclass of the builtin class `BaseException`\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8133770Z +               'However, it recommended that you only use subclasses of the builtin class `Exception` (which is itself a subclass of `BaseException`).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8133968Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8134069Z +               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8134195Z                 '## Recommendation\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8134878Z +               'Ensure that the specified class is the one intended. If it is not then replace it with the correct one. Otherwise the entire `except` block can be deleted.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8135857Z -               'If a `NotImplementedError` is intended to be raised, replace the use of `NotImplemented` with that. If `NotImplemented` is intended to be returned rather than raised, replace the `raise` with `return NotImplemented`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8135944Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8136025Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8136139Z                 '## Example\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8136823Z -               'In the following example, the method `wrong` will incorrectly raise a `TypeError` when called. The method `right` will raise a `NotImplementedError`.\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8136903Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8137000Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8137106Z                 '```python\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8137247Z +               'def handle_int():\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8137371Z +               '    try:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8137604Z +               '        raise_int()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8138051Z +               '    #This will not cause an exception, but it will be ignored\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8138223Z +               '    except int:\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8138429Z +               '        print("This will never be printed")\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8138515Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8138680Z -               'class Abstract(object):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8138761Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8138915Z -               '    def wrong(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8139192Z -               '        # Will raise a TypeError\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8139369Z -               '        raise NotImplemented()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8139467Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8139608Z -               '    def right(self):\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8139798Z -               '        raise NotImplementedError()\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8139893Z -               '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8139978Z                 '```\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8140063Z                 '\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8140181Z                 '## References\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8140767Z +               '* Python Language Reference: [Exceptions](https://docs.python.org/reference/executionmodel.html#exceptions).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8141273Z +               '* Python Tutorial: [Handling Exceptions](https://docs.python.org/tutorial/errors.html#handling-exceptions).\n'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8141919Z -               '* Python Language Reference: [The NotImplementedError exception](https://docs.python.org/library/exceptions.html#NotImplementedError).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8142510Z -               '* Python Language Reference: [The NotImplemented constant](https://docs.python.org/3/library/constants.html#NotImplemented).\n' +
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8143122Z -               '* Python Language Reference: [Emulating numeric types](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/datamodel.html#emulating-numeric-types).\n'
2026-10-20T21:06:14.8143206Z             },
